From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer, shell32: the desktop's icons and File Explorer follow a new display scale crisply

After a new display scale (0890) the desktop's icons, their titles and
their grid stayed the old scale's -- small at 175% -- and File Explorer,
aware of the system DPI, was Wine's scaled picture of itself at the old
scale (0891): soft. Now:

- The desktop lays its icons out again at the new scale (explorer follows
  it, 1121; the taskbar hands the change to the desktop window, which does
  not hear the broadcast), and takes each file's icon at the size it is
  drawn even when the shell's lists were made at another one.
- The shell's image lists are made again at the system DPI the process
  has now (the old lists are kept for views made before).
- The shell's folder view, in a per-monitor v2 window, lays itself out
  again when its parent changes DPI (WM_DPICHANGED_AFTERPARENT): its font,
  its icons, its items, its columns' widths.
- File Explorer is per-monitor v2 and lays itself out again on
  WM_DPICHANGED: its fonts, its S() sizes, the tree's rows, the panes'
  widths, This PC and Quick access with the new icons.

At 100% nothing changes.

Test: test/dpifollow-gate.sh parts 3 and 5 (mutants
SG_MUTANT_DESKTOP_ICONS_FIXED in desktop.c, SG_MUTANT_FE_SYSTEM_AWARE in
fileexplorer.c, SG_MUTANT_DEFVIEW_DPI_IGNORED in shlview.c,
SG_MUTANT_SHELL_ICONS_FIXED in iconcache.c); test/dpilive-gate.sh.
